$ 
\mathcal{M}_{n}^{(j)}$ does not depend on $X_{j}$, we obtain 
\begin{equation}
|\Psi _{j}-\mathbf{E}_{j}\{\Psi _{j}\}|=|\mu _{jn}(\Delta )-\mathbf{E} 
_{j}\{\mu _{jn}(\Delta )\}|\leq 2/n.  \label{cpj}
\end{equation} 
This and (\ref{mart}) with $p=2$ imply assertion (i) of the lemma with $ 
C^{(1)}=2^{4}C_{2}$.

To prove assertion (ii) we choose $p=1$ in (\ref{mart})  ,
